# Dermatologist Outreach Email Prompt

Use this prompt each time you have a new dermatologist or clinic to reach out to. Fill in the bracketed fields, paste the full thing in.

---

I'm Jyoti, editor at Mirellé Inspo (mirelleinspo.com), a nail-focused publication with ~32,000 monthly readers. I'm collecting dermatologist input for upcoming articles and want a personalized outreach email for the contact below.

**Contact details:**
- Name: [Full name, or "Clinic team" if no individual doctor is named]
- Email: [email address]
- Website / social links: [any URLs you have — clinic site, YouTube, Instagram, etc.]
- Article topic: [exact article title/topic for this outreach]
- Publish date: [date]
- Reply-by deadline: [date, ~5 days before publish]

**Before writing the email, do this:**
1. Check the website/social links I gave you. Tell me what you find — their specialty, tone/positioning, any stated stance on sponsorships or brand deals, follower/subscriber counts, any content directly relevant to the article topic.
2. Flag anything that changes the pitch: e.g. if they explicitly reject sponsorships, don't lead with a backlink offer. If it's a multi-doctor clinic with no named contact, address it to the team, not a person.
3. Tell me what personalization hook you'd use and why, before writing the full email — one sentence, so I can approve or correct it before you draft.

**Once I approve the hook, write the email using this structure:**
- Personalized opening line (from step 3, specific to this contact — never generic flattery)
- Who I am + the 32K reader stat, stated plainly, no exaggeration
- The specific article topic, framed as wanting real clinical input instead of generic recycled advice
- The ask: a few questions answered in writing, no call needed, they can answer as much or as little as they like. Say I'll send exact questions once they confirm — do not include placeholder questions in the email.
- What's offered in return: match this to what I told you in the research step (backlink + socials if commercially oriented, byline-only if they reject sponsorships/brand deals, mention paid collaboration as a secondary, softer option if their time is billed — e.g. consultation fees)
- Publish date and reply-by deadline, stated together
- Soft close: fine if timing doesn't work, just reply either way

**Formatting rules — always follow these:**
- No em dashes, anywhere
- Plain, direct sentences, no fluff or overly salesy language
- Keep it under 200 words
- Sign off as: Jyoti, Editor, Mirellé Inspo, [site link]

**Output:** give me the finished subject line and email body, plus a one-line flag of any risk you see (e.g. "email format looks unverified," "no individual contact so response rate may be lower," "site suggests they may prefer a phone call over written Q&A").
